# Message-board.md is an append-only log written by several agents working in
# the same checkout. Without a merge driver, every concurrent append collides
# and an agent has to hand-resolve a conflict block that can span the whole
# file -- which is how entries get dropped.
#
# `union` is a built-in git merge driver: on conflict it keeps both sides
# instead of emitting markers. That is the correct semantics for a log, where
# no entry is ever wrong, only missing. Verified against both `git merge` and
# `git rebase`, including the case where one side adds three entries and the
# other one.
#
# This does NOT protect against a lost update on a *clean* apply: if an agent
# commits a snapshot of the board it read before someone else's push, the
# driver never sees a conflict. tests/contract/test_message_board_integrity.py
# catches that case by watching the entry count for regressions.
Message-board.md merge=union

# POSIX shell scripts must stay LF in both the blob and the checkout. Several
# are bind-mounted into containers or run under bash, and bash refuses scripts
# with CRLF endings (`$'\r': command not found`). The docker compose dev stack
# restart-looped Kafka on a fresh clone exactly this way (2026-11-10) because
# these files were committed with CRLF. `eol=lf` overrides any developer's
# `core.autocrlf`, so a Windows checkout cannot convert them back.
*.sh text eol=lf
